- '@id': https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/staff-domain/care-home
  route: staff-domain/care-home
  key: care-home
  '@type':
  - skos:Concept
  - dwp:ChangeOfCircumstance
  label: Permanent care-home residence
  definition: 'Permanent and temporary care-home stays require different Pension Credit household and component
    checks. DMG 78088 is under the heading Claimants who have no partner (including self-funders): all severe-disability-addition
    conditions still apply, including actual qualifying-benefit receipt. One partner entering permanently and both
    partners living permanently in a home require the separate DMG 77128–77130 household branches. Funding alone
    does not determine the whole credit.'
  aliases:
  - Care Home
  - Care Homes
  - care home permanently
  - permanently into a care home
  source_candidates:
  - source-c028
  - source-c030
  - source-c010
  required_concepts:
  - household-separation
  review_status: unreviewed-specialist-review-required
- '@id': https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/staff-domain/partner
  route: staff-domain/partner
  key: partner
  '@type':
  - skos:Concept
  - dwp:Circumstance
  label: Partner and household membership
  definition: Pension Credit couple status requires the DMG 77013 definition and household facts. Temporary
    absence, one partner entering a care home permanently, both partners living there, and mixed-age status
    are distinct conditional branches. Shared accommodation alone does not establish a shared household; the
    DMG 77130 factors are non-exhaustive and none alone decides the question.
  aliases:
  - partner
  - partners
  - couple
  source_candidates:
  - source-c009
  - source-c010
  - source-c011
  - source-c031
  review_status: unreviewed-specialist-review-required
