- '@id': https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/staff-domain/care-home-housing-costs
  route: staff-domain/care-home-housing-costs
  key: care-home-housing-costs
  '@type':
  - skos:Concept
  - dwp:BenefitComponent
  label: Pension Credit housing costs during care-home absence
  definition: DMG 78270 concerns the housing-cost additional amount, not the whole Pension Credit award. It
    states that an additional amount for housing costs is not allowed for claimants in a care home unless
    their absence from the dwelling normally occupied as home is temporary. The exception does not establish
    payment of care-home fees. DMG 78240 allows treatment as living in the former home, with housing costs
    allowed, for a trial period of up to 13 weeks, subject to assessment of suitability, intention to return
    if unsuitable and the normally occupied part of the home not being let or sublet. This temporary-absence
    treatment is subject to the stated overall maximum of 52 weeks. DMG
    78254–78257 set separate 52-week conditions including intention to return, no letting or subletting, a
    listed reason and expected duration. Permanent residence and Housing Benefit expenditure are separate
    exclusions. DMG 78271 defines Housing Benefit expenditure as an element for which Housing Benefit may be
    payable; actual payment of Housing Benefit is not stated as a condition here. The complete paragraphs
    span adjacent pages.
  aliases:
  - care-home housing costs
  - trial care-home stay
  source_candidates:
  - source-c030
  required_source_ids:
  - https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/page/78/0053
  - https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/page/78/0055
  - https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/page/78/0056
  - https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/page/78/0057
  - https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/page/78/0058
